From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:45:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] buttons: support PM6150-class power-on blocks and other PMIC
 layouts

The driver only knew the PMK8350's power-on block (subtype 9, "gen3")
at peripheral 0x013 and volume up on GPIO6 of the PM7325. On older
PMICs such as the PM6150 (SM7150, the Mi 9T) the power-on block has
subtype 1 to 5 and reports KPDPWR and RESIN in bits 0 and 1 instead of
7 and 6 (Linux pm8941-pwrkey.c, qpnp-power-on.c).

- Accept subtypes 1-5 and 9 and pick the key bits from the subtype.
- Take the peripherals from boot-args pmic_pon= and pmic_volume_up=
  (slave << 8 | peripheral); the defaults stay redwood's.

Tested on the Mi 9T with the old port (pmic_pon=0x008,
pmic_volume_up=0x4c1): power and both volume keys work. Redwood's
behaviour is unchanged when the arguments are absent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
